  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">TA-9781 REG: Developing South Asian Livable Cities Facility - Aged Care Service Specialist (42173-015)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Review all policies, institutional frameworks, publications, demographic and health data relevant to older persons and aged care and identify key areas for policy and program reforms, including improvement in competencies and capacities of the social workforce that will manage the protection and care facilities to be established under this project</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support project design, incorporating lessons and experiences from similar projects on aged care services</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support the Gender Specialist/Team Leader consultant in consultation meetings with key government agencies (i.e., MGFSS, MOH, FPA, Maldives Police) and CSOs, with focus on strengthening protection and care and support services for older persons</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The aged care services specialist will be part of a project preparatory team to conduct due diligence (technical, economic, financial, environmental and social safeguards, institutional, and gender assessments) for a proposed grant to Maldives for Strengthening Gender Inclusive Initiatives.The consultant will work in close collaboration with the Team Leader and other due diligence consultants, and report to the ADB project officer. He/She will support, coordinate, and supervise the inputs from all team members and take responsibility for high-quality study outputs and deliverables. The consultant will (i) assist in preparing the RRP, linked documents and TORs for the proposed Strengthening Gender Inclusive Initiatives project; (ii) undertake analysis on existing care and support services to older persons including, but not limited to government legislation and policy, human resources, financing, quality management and infrastructure; (iii) review of policies, institutional frameworks and publications relevant to aged  care; (iv) provide practical recommendations for improvements to community-based aged  care in the Maldives with focus on feasible and efficient operational arrangements including potential private or civil society organisations engagement and flexible service delivery; (v) input on the structural design of the aged  care centers to ensure facilities are responsive to the intended services that will be provided; and (vi) support capacity building on social protection to older persons,. The consultant will be responsible for undertaking detailed sector assessments and support the overall investment project design, scope, and documentation in accordance with ADB guidelines.</narrative>
  </description>
